Bundled data files
------------------

naaulu/data/radars_wmo.json
naaulu/data/radars.json
    Derived from the World Meteorological Organization (WMO) Weather Radar
    Database, maintained on behalf of WMO by the Turkish State Meteorological
    Service (TSMS): https://wrd.mgm.gov.tr
    Licence: CC BY-SA 4.0
    Attribution: "World Meteorological Organization (WMO)"

naaulu/data/ne_50m_admin_0_countries.geojson
naaulu/data/ne_10m_admin_0_countries.geojson
    Natural Earth. Public domain; no credit required.

naaulu/data/radars_usa.json
naaulu/data/radars_aus.json
naaulu/data/radars_opera.json
naaulu/data/chmi_aws_stations.json
    Compiled from public-sector sources (NOAA, Bureau of Meteorology via NCI,
    EUMETNET OPERA, CHMI). See docs/data-sources.md for the provider and
    licence of each.

Administrative boundaries are not bundled: the country outlines drawn with
--adm 2/--adm 3 (ADM0), the province tier drawn with --adm 2 (ADM2) and the
city labels of --adm 3 are filled from Geofabrik Postpass queries into
OpenStreetMap (ODbL, credit "© OpenStreetMap contributors") — by
prefetch_boundaries.py at build time or on a plot's first use — cached in
the user data directory, with the source and licence of every file
recorded in a .meta.json next to it. The windows and country outlines used at --adm 1
come from the bundled Natural Earth file (naaulu/data/
ne_10m_admin_0_countries.geojson; public domain, no credit required).
